5. **Theoretical guarantees are lacking.** While the divergence-free property is guaranteed by construction, there are no convergence analyses or error bounds for the advection scheme. The covariant derivative approximation in Eq. 15 uses a first-order approximation (taking t=h/2), but no analysis of the approximation error or its effect on long-term stability is provided. As noted in a review of a related neural PDE method, "the theoretical guarantees are limited... there are no guarantees about approximation capabilities or convergence" and "a theoretical analysis of convergence and stability of our method would be valuable" ( Neural Superposition Networks review, Reviewer 3; the paper itself acknowledges this as future work).

